    "done_when": "The review of a-reused-snapshot-takes-the-callers-stall-window (90, merged at 99d6fc41f) found a gap. The budget_seconds the snapshot carries (reckon/crew/recovery.py, about line 8454) is what keeps reuse equal to a full recompute when a live child widens the stall window to the run's declared budget. No test exercises a live child: dropping that one line leaves both new cases green. The node adds a case to tests/test_a_reused_snapshot_takes_the_callers_stall_window.py. The case builds a snapshot with process_alive True, process_descendant_alive True and a declared budget_seconds well above the caller's stall_seconds. It reads the snapshot back through reuse at a moment past stall_seconds but inside the budget, and asserts the state equals a full recompute's, not stalled. It changes no product file. The declared negative control, removing the budget_seconds carry from the snapshot, must make the new case fail; it is executed and logged. The file passes.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.5,
